{"requirements":[{"id":"mail-routing","requirement":"Mail sent from node2 to helpdesk@branch.test reaches both alice and bob, while accounts@branch.test reaches bob only.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final post-restart SMTP submissions were accepted. Mailbox tokens and delivery logs directly show helpdesk delivery to alice and bob, accounts delivery to bob, and no accounts token in alice's mailbox.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0c14f28ce10b469f","cmd-1f82ca649946421e","cmd-11ed3a04abad4f5a"]},{"id":"smtp-rejections","requirement":"Unknown branch.test recipients and relay attempts to unrelated domains are rejected.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final tests from node2 received 550 for an unknown local recipient and 554 Relay access denied for an unrelated domain; node1 logs independently record both rejections.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0c14f28ce10b469f","cmd-1f82ca649946421e"]},{"id":"handover-preservation","requirement":"Preserve the sample message and routing handover under /srv/legacy2/smtp-alias-delivery.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both files retained their original SHA-256 hashes, permissions, ownership, and sizes on node1 and node2 through the completed restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-0c14f28ce10b469f","cmd-1f82ca649946421e"]},{"id":"platform-preservation","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0. Node1 used the signed RHEL repository Postfix 3.8.5 package, which operated successfully after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-50bee822ccff4a19","cmd-c038dd35baa0411a","cmd-0c14f28ce10b469f","cmd-1f82ca649946421e","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Package installation and trusted-key import, account creation, Postfix/alias/firewall configuration, SELinux relabeling, bounded delivery tests, and both restarts each supported task completion or mandatory evidence. The extracted temporary key was removed; the retained root-only rollback snapshot has a clear recovery purpose. Final lifecycle observations show no failed services and healthy package-manager state on either node.","evidence_ids":["cmd-08af3db933c94328","cmd-50bee822ccff4a19","cmd-81d86139f0ec49b4","cmd-1f82ca649946421e","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All four material outcomes are satisfied with direct final behavior. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identities, recovered services and data, and successful final SMTP behavior. Fixed lifecycle boot identities corroborate both restarts.","limitations":["The stdout captured for cmd-1f82ca649946421e is truncated near part of the mailbox report, but its visible delivery logs and the independent mailbox evidence in cmd-11ed3a04abad4f5a cover the omitted detail."]}
